        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Gasquet, Tatiana Golovin, Jim Pugh\n- Roles: professional tennis player, doubles specialist\n- Events: 2004 French Open, Grand Slam tournaments\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Gasquet won the mixed doubles Grand Slam title at the 2004 French Open with Tatiana Golovin as his partner.\n- Jim Pugh was born on February 5, 1964, in Burbank, California, and he is a former professional tennis player from the United States.\n- Jim Pugh specialized in doubles and won three Grand Slam men's doubles titles, including two Australian Open titles and one Wimbledon title.\n- Jim Pugh also won five Grand Slam mixed doubles titles, including three Australian Open titles, one Wimbledon title, and one US Open title.",
